 AMOUNT OF \nEARNINGS (if any) and PAY IT TO THE LEVYING OFFICER during the \nwithholding period.\n(A) To determine the CORRECT AMOUNT OF EARNINGS TO BE WITH- \nHELD (if any), first compute the employee's disposable earnings.\nEarnings \ninclude \nany \nmoney \n(whether \ncalled \nwages, \nsalary, \ncommissions, bonuses, or anything else) that is paid by an employer to  an \nemployee for personal services. Vacation or sick pay is subject to \nwithholding as it is received by the employee. Tips are generally not \nincluded as earnings because they are not paid by the employer.\nDisposable earnings are the earnings left after subtracting the part of the \n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n| California Courts | Self Help Guide (https://selfhelp.courts.ca.gov/find-forms/latest-changes)\nciteturn1732search1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 5 days ago; CARE-125  | New  | Court Referral to the CARE Act Court ... WG-030  | Revised  | Earnings Withholding Order for Elder and Dependent Adult Financial Abuse\nWG-022  | Revised  | Earnings Withholding Order for Taxes (Wage Garnishment-State Tax Liability)\nWG-030  | Revised  | Earnings Withholding Order for Elder and Dependent Adult Financial Abuse\n\n## Forms Approved 10/24/2025, Effective 01/01/2026\n\n## [Button: Adoption]\n\nADOPT-050-INFO  | Revised  | How to Adopt a Child in California\nADOPT-205  | Revised  | Declaration Confirming Parentage in Stepparent Adoption\nADOPT-206  | Revised  | Declaration Confirming Parentage in Stepparent Adoption: Gestational Surrogacy\n\n## [Button: CARE Act]\n\nCARE-105  | Revised  | Order for CARE Act Report\nCARE-106  | Revised  | Notice of Order for CARE Act Report\nCARE-107  | Revised  | Proof of Personal Service of Notice of Order for CARE Act Report\nCARE-110  | Revised  | Notice of Initial Appearance—CARE Act Proceedings\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nI N V I T A T I O N T O C O M M E N T 